<section class="band band--night">
  <div class="shell">
    <h2>Who tends to work well here</h2>
    <div class="cards">
      <div>
        <h3>The associate who wants more than hours</h3>
        <p>You could get cheaper supervision. What you want is someone who will tell you what
        actually happened in that session, and help you build something after licensure.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3>The therapist whose EMDR keeps stalling</h3>
        <p>Preparation looks fine, then processing floods or flatlines. Usually that is a part
        of the client objecting, and it is workable once you can see it.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3>The clinician running on empty</h3>
        <p>Competent, respected, quietly depleted. You teach regulation skills you no longer
        practice. That is what the retreats are for.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3>The one drawn to body-based work</h3>
        <p>You have read about somatic approaches and want to practice inside one, with a
        supervisor who works that way every week rather than recommending it.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

